## Violations and Termination

On Licensor's first written notice identifying a violation of this license, your licenses under this document continue for 32 days after you receive the notice, but only for acts within the grant. They continue afterward only if you fully comply and take practical steps to correct the identified past violations within that period. Otherwise they terminate at its end. After you complete that first cure, a new violation terminates your licenses under this document immediately. Earlier conduct disclosed or discovered during the first cure period does not alone count as a new violation. The separate immediate patent-termination provision remains effective. After termination, stop acts requiring this license and delete copies held only under it.

During a cure period, only acts within the grant are licensed. Cure does not authorize past copying outside the grant. An Organization never receives a license or a free trial through this cure provision. Separate MIT, GitHub, and statutory rights remain unaffected.

